[Desktop Entry]
Name=sol
Comment=Your desktop is the solar system
Exec=sol-session
TryExec=sol-session
Type=Application
DesktopNames=sol;driftwm
Keywords=canvas;infinite;wayland;driftwm;solar system

# What a login screen reads to offer sol beside every other desktop on the
# machine. Without it there is no way to choose sol except booting specially,
# which is a strange thing to ask of someone who just wants to try it — and a
# stranger thing to ask of someone who wants to go back to KDE afterwards.
#
# DesktopNames becomes XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, which is how everything else on
# the system finds out which desktop it is running under: portals pick their
# backend by it, applications pick their file dialogs by it, and
# `sol-portals.conf` beside this file is named for the first entry.
#
# `sol` first and `driftwm` second, because they are two different questions.
# Applications asking "which desktop" want the session; anything that cares
# about the compositor underneath can look past the semicolon.
